# Why this rule exists

The team decided to standardize on ChromaDB as the only vector store 
for all memory storage and retrieval operations. This ensures consistency 
across the entire FME pipeline.

# Rule

Always use ChromaDB for all vector storage and memory retrieval. 
Do not introduce PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Pinecone, Weaviate, or any 
other database for memory operations.

# Checklist

- Use ChromaDB for all memory storage operations
- Do not add any other vector store or database dependency
- All memory retrieval must go through ChromaDB HNSW search

# Related technologies

- ChromaDB
